{
  "_note": "Generated from the Move declarations under sources/events/, with the JSON encoding rules verified against live Sui mainnet GraphQL on 2026-08-26. These are the shapes an off-chain decoder must accept. The vector<u8> encoding was settled in s6 against published testnet package 0x109fba1479e19843b2b6ed8d225b9fb341c85cc274ca5ae90bcf40242f0c7a0b, on six live events read back both from the executing client and from the fullnode; every other rule still comes from the 2026-08-26 mainnet GraphQL run.",
  "_encoding": {
    "bool": "JSON boolean",
    "u8 / u16 / u32": "JSON number",
    "u64 / u128 / u256": "JSON string, because the value can exceed 2^53",
    "address": "0x-prefixed 32-byte hex string",
    "ID": "0x-prefixed 32-byte hex string",
    "std::string::String": "JSON string",
    "Option<T>": "T's encoding, or null when none",
    "vector<T>": "JSON array of T's encoding",
    "vector<u8>": "CONFIRMED (s6, testnet). Base64 JSON string, NOT an array of numbers. A 32-byte commit sent as 00112233445566778899aabbccddeeff twice reads back as \"ABEiM0RVZneImaq7zN3u/wARIjNEVWZ3iJmqu8zd7v8=\". This is a special case: vector<u16> and vector<ID> are still arrays. A decoder must base64-decode every `commit`, `previous_commit` and any other vector<u8> field."
  },
  "_filters": {
    "grpc": "EventTypeFilter { event_type: \"<PACKAGE>\" } returns every event the protocol raises, whichever module declares it.",
    "graphql": "events(filter: { type: \"<PACKAGE>\" }) , the same.",
    "json_rpc": "suix_queryEvents is deactivated on public fullnodes as of 2026-08-26 and returns -32601 Method not found."
  },
